# The user's ~/.gitignore_global excludes CLAUDE.md / GEMINI.md / FOR_ME.md /
# REPO_PARSE.md in EVERY repo, which is right for source repos — it stops a
# personal instruction file being committed into someone else's project.
#
# It is wrong HERE. This repo's whole job is to distribute those files, and the
# rule silently kept dot_claude/CLAUDE.md untracked for months: chezmoi managed
# it, `chezmoi status` showed it pending, but git never carried it, so it reached
# no other machine. Negate the rule for the files this repo exists to ship.
!CLAUDE.md
!GEMINI.md
!dot_claude/CLAUDE.md
!dot_gemini/GEMINI.md
